<section class="project-section" id="assembly" aria-labelledby="assembly-title">
  <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">The joint determines the motion</p><h2 id="assembly-title">Assembly sequence</h2><p>Grasp a unit, align its connection, and engage the joint.</p></div>
  <ol class="method-steps numbered"><li><span aria-hidden="true">01</span><h3>Pick up</h3><p>Establish a grasp for the module’s geometry.</p></li><li><span aria-hidden="true">02</span><h3>Align</h3><p>Orient the unit relative to the existing structure.</p></li><li><span aria-hidden="true">03</span><h3>Interlock</h3><p>Place or slide the module into its joint.</p></li></ol>
  <Figure id="connections" />
</section>
<section class="project-section" id="concept" aria-labelledby="concept-title">
  <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Gulf Futures Challenge</p><h2 id="concept-title">Coastal application</h2><p>The supplied AMERICA presentation brings design, materials, and construction together.</p></div>
  <Figure id="coastal-overview" />
  <p class="scope-note">Concept illustrations and a manufacturing reference. Assembly experiments and coastal performance measurements are not part of the materials presented here.</p>
</section>
